   <text:p text:style-name="P478">Func<text:span text:style-name="T1281">t</text:span>i<text:span text:style-name="T1120">on</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P756">They flip the image horizontally and vertically, respectively.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P135">Shortcut<text:span text:style-name="T1420">s</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1748"><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T1">H</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> (horizontal) </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T231">and</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T1">J</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> (vertical)</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P482"><text:soft-page-break/>Mode <text:span text:style-name="T1120">of operation</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P480">Select the viewer where the transformation has to be applied and press the <text:span text:style-name="T1281">toolbar button </text:span>or the corresponding shortcut.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P482">V<text:span text:style-name="T1120">iewer where it is applied</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P758">The active viewer (with the blue frame).</text:p>
