   <text:p text:style-name="P487">Func<text:span text:style-name="T1283">t</text:span>i<text:span text:style-name="T1122">on</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P681"><text:span text:style-name="T1283">It returns the viewer to its initial state as if it was reloaded from the beginning, returning to the initial slice and phase, to the initial window, undoing rotations and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1284">zooms, erasing measurements, etc.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P137">Shortcut</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1754"><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T1">Ctrl</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T1">R</text:span></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P487">Mode <text:span text:style-name="T1123">of operation</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P491">Select the viewer that has to be restored and press the <text:span text:style-name="T1285">toolbar button </text:span>or the shortcut.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P487">Vi<text:span text:style-name="T1123">ewer where it is applied</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P759">The active viewer (with the blue frame).</text:p>
