   <text:p text:style-name="P487">Func<text:span text:style-name="T1287">t</text:span>i<text:span text:style-name="T1124">on</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P490">It <text:span text:style-name="T1287">shows or </text:span>hides the textual information <text:span text:style-name="T1287">with</text:span>in the viewers, <text:span text:style-name="T1287">including </text:span>patient and study data, <text:span text:style-name="T1287">image data, image size, current window, slice, orientation, etc</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P493"><text:span text:style-name="T1287">This feature is useful if one needs to create an image </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T915">to present it</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1287"> without patient data.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P825"><text:span text:style-name="T1287">Information printed on the image itself cannot be hidden, as is often the case </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T915">with</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1287"> ultrasounds, amongst others.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P2263"><text:span text:style-name="T1443">You can configure what information is shown for each modality as explained in section </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1443"><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="chapter" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc47686_1825085122">16.3</text:bookmark-ref></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1443"><text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1443"><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc47686_1825085122">2D viewer annotations</text:bookmark-ref></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1443">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P138">Shortcut</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1769"><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T1">.</text:span></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P885">Mode <text:span text:style-name="T1125">of operation</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P2056"><text:span text:style-name="T100">C</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T234">lick</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T100"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T67"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T100"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T234">on the toolbar button to hide the information and click</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T100"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T67"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T100"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T238">on it another time</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T234"> to show </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T238">the information</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T234"> again. Alternatively, the shortcut can be used. By default, textual information is visible unless otherwise stated in the</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T97"> </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#1.13.1.Visor 2D|outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T234">settings</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T97">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P494">Vi<text:span text:style-name="T1126">ewer where it is applied</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P492"><text:span text:style-name="T1288">All of them</text:span>.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1037"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Marc13" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="17cm" style:rel-width="100%" draw:z-index="394">
     <draw:text-box fo:min-height="0.041cm">
