   <text:p text:style-name="P893">Func<text:span text:style-name="T1336">t</text:span>i<text:span text:style-name="T1158">on</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P771">It allows marking a point of the image in a viewer and displaying the corresponding position in the other viewers.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P149">Shortcut</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1836"><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T1">C</text:span></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P893"><text:soft-page-break/>Mode <text:span text:style-name="T1159">of operation</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P2076"><text:span text:style-name="T115">C</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T271">lick</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T115"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T67"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T115"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T356">on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T271">the toolbar button or press the shortcut to enable the 3D cursor. Then click</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T115"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T67"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T115"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T271">on a point in the image of a viewer and the same point will be marked with a cross </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T343">hairs</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T271"> in all the other viewers that meet a condition, changing the displayed slice if needed. It is also possible to drag the mouse while holding down the left button</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T116"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T67"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T116"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T271">so that the other viewers are updated in real time. The condition for another viewer to be updated is that the series it displays is from the same study and has the same Frame of Reference UID (0020,0052) (this is usually the case if the patient has not moved between the series’ generation). To disable the 3D cursor, another tool has to be enabled.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P895">Vi<text:span text:style-name="T1160">ewer where it is applied</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P770">All those that meet the aforementioned condition.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1037"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr4" draw:name="Marc19" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="17cm" style:rel-width="100%" draw:z-index="442">
