   <text:p text:style-name="P598"><text:span text:style-name="T1361">Where</text:span>:</text:p>
   <text:list xml:id="list151014251037624" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="List_20_1">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2410"><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T1">T</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T953">1/2</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T299">is the half-life in seconds</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2410"><text:span text:style-name="T299">The calculation of</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T1">Δt</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T299">is given according to the value of the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">Decay Correction (0054,1102) </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T299">DICOM attribute</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">:</text:span></text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P2410"><text:span text:style-name="T299">If it is </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T1">START</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">: </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T1">Δt</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T299">is the time interval between the administration of the dose and the acquisition of the image, in seconds</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P2410"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T299">If it is</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T1">ADMIN</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">: </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Citation"><text:span text:style-name="T1">Δt</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T299">is</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> 0</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P822">The calculation of the time interval is preferably done with the Series Date (0008,0021), Series Time (0008,0031) a<text:span text:style-name="T1422">n</text:span>d Radiopharmaceutical Start Date Time (0018,1078) attributes.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P825"><text:span text:style-name="T1361">If they are not available, it is done </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1362">with the Series Time (0008,0031) and Radiopharmaceutical Start Time (0018,107</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T928">2</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1362">) attributes, assuming that the administration of the dose and the acquisition of the images have been done the same day.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P716">If any of these attributes is also missing, the calculation of the SUV cannot be carried out.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P717" text:outline-level="5"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc29918_4233914545"/>Lean body mass<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc29918_4233914545"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P715">The lean body mass is calculated with two formulae<text:span text:style-name="T957">, Morga</text:span>n’s<text:span text:style-name="T957"><text:note text:id="ftn11" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>11</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
       <text:p text:style-name="P2104"><text:span text:style-name="T366">D</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T367">enis J. Morgan, Kelly M. Bray. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Definition"><text:span text:style-name="T367">Lean body mass as a predictor of drug dosage. Implications for drug therapy.</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T367"> Clinical Pharmacokinetics. 1994, Vol. 26, 4, pp. 292–307. </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://doi.org/10.2165/00003088-199426040-00005" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T1">https://doi.org/10.2165/00003088-199426040-00005</text:span></text:a></text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T957"> o</text:span>r<text:span text:style-name="T957"> Jame</text:span>s<text:span text:style-name="T957">’</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T957"><text:note text:id="ftn12" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>12</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
       <text:p text:style-name="P2103"><text:span text:style-name="T1">W. Philip T. James. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Definition"><text:span text:style-name="T47">Research on obesity.</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T47"> London: Her Majesty’s Stationery Office, 1976. ISBN 0114500347.</text:span></text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T957">, </text:span>depending on the patient’s <text:span text:style-name="T1365">sex</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T957">:</text:span></text:p>
   <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="List_20_1">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2367"><text:span text:style-name="T1362">Males</text:span> (Morgan): <text:span text:style-name="T956"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr57" draw:name="Objecte3" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.681cm" svg:width="4.852cm" svg:height="1.124cm" draw:z-index="550"><draw:object>
         <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
          <semantics>
           <mrow>
            <mi mathvariant="italic">LBM</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">=</mo>
            <mrow>
             <mrow>
              <mn>1.1</mn>
              <mo stretchy="false">×</mo>
              <mi>W</mi>
             </mrow>
             <mo stretchy="false">−</mo>
             <mrow>
              <mn>120</mn>
              <mo stretchy="false">×</mo>
              <msup>
               <mrow>
                <mo fence="true" form="prefix" stretchy="true">(</mo>
                <mrow>
                 <mfrac>
                  <mi>W</mi>
                  <mi>H</mi>
                 </mfrac>
                </mrow>
                <mo fence="true" form="postfix" stretchy="true">)</mo>
               </mrow>
               <mn>2</mn>
              </msup>
             </mrow>
            </mrow>
           </mrow>
           <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">LBM = 1.1 times W - 120 times left( W over H right)^2</annotation>
          </semantics>
         </math>
        </draw:object><draw:image>
