     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T1375">If </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1376">one opens a study containing one or more series with encapsulated PDF, the PDF extension will be opened. It contains a list of icons representing the different encapsulated PDF contained in the study.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1311"><text:span text:style-name="T1">By double-clicking</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T312"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T134"></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T312"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">on one of the icons, the corresponding PDF is </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T354">de-</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T311">encapsulated and opened with the system’s default PDF viewer.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P1372" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc4886_1692806117"/>Diagnosis tests<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc4886_1692806117"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1040">Diagnosis tests allow to check if Starviewer and its environment are properly configured and the hardware meets the minimum requirements.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P2090"><text:span text:style-name="T1">To access the diagnosis tests, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T311">go to</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> the</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T135"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Display"><text:span text:style-name="T311">T</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Display"><text:span text:style-name="T815">ools</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Display"><text:span text:style-name="T135"> &gt; </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Display"><text:span text:style-name="T311">Run diagnosis tests</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> menu. Its functionality is to verify a series of system parameters and run a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T311">set</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> of tests that allow </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T311">evaluating</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> whether the system is well configured </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T354">and</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T311">meets</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> the recommended requirements, and diagnos</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T354">ing</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> errors and possible problems.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P611"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr11" draw:name="Imatge165" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="13.284cm" svg:height="2.566cm" draw:z-index="501"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
