       </draw:g><text:span text:style-name="Caption_20_characters"><text:span text:style-name="T1">D</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Caption_20_characters"><text:span text:style-name="T1227">rawing</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Caption_20_characters"><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Caption_20_characters"><text:span text:style-name="T1"><text:sequence text:ref-name="refDrawing1" text:name="Drawing" text:formula="ooow:Drawing+1" style:num-format="1">2</text:sequence></text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="Caption_20_characters"><text:span text:style-name="T1">:</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T332">Another example of maximisation to multiple screens. On the left the window is displayed in black and the screen layout in blue, in the initial state. On the right the result of maximising to multiple screens; the window has expanded taking up six screens, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T333">two wide and three high.</text:span></text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame><text:soft-page-break/>This feature adjusts the size of the Starviewer window so that it takes up the maximum number of screens as long as they together form a rectangular space. Horizontal expansion is first considered, and then the vertical one.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P624"><text:span text:style-name="T1392">Keep in mind that for the expansion to work, the screens must have exactly the same number of pixels </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T925">at</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1392"> the edges </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1393">that touch each other</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1392">. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T924">Otherwise</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1392">, a rectangular shape is not detected.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P732" text:outline-level="4"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc24550_1084088360"/>Move to previous screen<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc24550_1084088360"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1943"><text:span text:style-name="T334">Shortcut</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T143">: </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T143">Ctrl</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T143">+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T143">Shift</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T143">+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T143">←</text:span></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P731">This function moves the window to the previous screen following a circular sequence as in Drawing<text:span text:style-name="T1064"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1064"><text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="value" text:ref-name="refDrawing2">3</text:sequence-ref></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T969">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P733" text:outline-level="4"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc24552_1084088360"/>Move to next screen<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc24552_1084088360"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1950"><text:span text:style-name="T334">Shortcut</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T144">: </text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T144">Ctrl</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T144">+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T144">Shift</text:span></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T144">+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="Keyboard"><text:span text:style-name="T143">→</text:span></text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P627"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Marc35" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="17cm" style:rel-width="100%" draw:z-index="521">
