    </draw:frame><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc41284_573806592"/>2D viewer layout<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc41284_573806592"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P271">This section allows configuring how the 2D viewer images are <text:span text:style-name="T1402">laid out</text:span> when a study is opened depending on the modality. There is a tab for each modality.</text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Taula9" table:style-name="Taula9">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Taula9.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Taula9.B"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Taula9.C"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P110">Op<text:span text:style-name="T1401">t</text:span>ions</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P101">D<text:span text:style-name="T958">escrip</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1401">t</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T958">i</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1401">on</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P120">Default value</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P270">Use hanging protocols if available</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P1444"><text:span text:style-name="T131">I</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T345">f it is enabled and a study of the modality is opened, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T346">priority will be given to </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T345">applying the best applicable</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T151"> </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#1.8.1.1.1.Hanging protocols|outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T151">hanging protocol</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T345">. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T346">If it is disabled or there is no applicable hanging protocol, an</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T151"> </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#1.8.1.1.2.Distribució automàtica|outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T346">automatic regular layout</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T151"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T346">will be applied according to the parameters described in the following points.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.C2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P211"><text:span text:style-name="T1402">Enabled for</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T974"> CR, CT, MG, MR </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1402">and</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T974"> US</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A3" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P273">Layout by</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.B3" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P273">If the layout is by series, each viewer is assigned a different series, <text:span text:style-name="T1403">sorted by series number. If the layout is by images, each viewer is assigned a different image, regardless of the series, sorted by series number and image number within the series.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.C3" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P224">S<text:span text:style-name="T1403">er</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T974">ies </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1403">for</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T974"> CT, MR, NM, PT, SC </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1403">and</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T974"> XA; images </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1403">for the rest</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T974">.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A4" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P274">Layout direction</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.B4" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P274">It decides in which order the viewers of the grid are filled: by rows (left to right) or by columns (top to bottom). Always starting with the top-left viewer.</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.C4" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P275">Left to right</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A4" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P274">Exclude from layout</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.B5" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P276"><text:span text:style-name="T1403">It allows excluding some types of image</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1404">s from the regular layout that are</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1403"> considered </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1404">little relevant.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.C5" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P225"><text:span text:style-name="T1404">CT localisers</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T975"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1404">and</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1094"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1404">CT attenuation correction (B08s) enabled for CT, and MR surveys enabled for MR</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A6" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P277">Maximum number of viewers</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.B6" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P225">Maximum number of viewers that will be created <text:span text:style-name="T1405">with the automatic layout when the study is opened. No more viewers will be created even if there are series or images left to view. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1407">M</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1406">ore </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1407">viewers</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1406"> than necessary will </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1407">also n</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1406">ever be created if there are few series or images.</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.C6" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P225"><text:span text:style-name="T1407">As many as possible</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T975"> (equivalent </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1407">to</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T975"> 48)</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Taula9.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.A7" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P217">R<text:span text:style-name="T975">est</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1407">ore defaults</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.B7" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P302">It restores the default values of the selected modality.</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Taula9.C7" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P232"/>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P2259">The last option, independent of modality, is <text:span text:style-name="Citation">Division when comparing studies</text:span> and allows to choose how the window is divided in two halves when the <text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc2921_831695085">Comparison of studies</text:bookmark-ref><text:s/>is activated. There are the following options:</text:p>
   <text:list xml:id="list151014243077116" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="List_20_1">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2421"><text:span text:style-name="Citation">Current left, prior right</text:span> (default)</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2421"><text:span text:style-name="Citation">Current right, prior left</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2421"><text:span text:style-name="Citation">Current top, prior bottom</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P2421"><text:span text:style-name="Citation">Current bottom, prior top</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:h text:style-name="P1043" text:outline-level="3"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr11" draw:name="Imatge212" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="17cm" svg:height="11.515cm" draw:z-index="536"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
